dante-server (1.4.2+dfsg-4) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  The danted.service file now enables several hardening options:
  PrivateTmp, InaccessibleDirectories, ReadOnlyDirectories, and
  DeviceAllow.  If the default values specified in the service file are
  not suitable for a specific installation, they may be overridden by
  using the "drop-in directory" mechanism as described in
  the https://wiki.debian.org/systemd#Creating_or_altering_services and
  https://manpages.debian.org/man/5/systemd.unit documentation.

 -- Peter Pentchev <roam@debian.org>  Sat, 15 Sep 2018 13:36:05 +0300
